Save the character sets with the cursor, and answer DECRQM for ANSI modes

DECSC saves the character sets on every DEC terminal; here a program that
restored its cursor kept whatever set was selected. Carried beside saved
and saved_primary and swapped with them, and dumped as table indexes like
the live ones, since an encoding is a pointer.

DECRQM without the ? had no case at all, so a program asking about IRM or
LNM waited for an answer that never came. Mode 47 and 1048 are reported.

